                <pb facs="0623" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.6511/154: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-25T18:00:00-04:00">September 25, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>318. Department’s 315, September 24, 7 p.m. Jones has agreed to the flat 4
                    percent per annum interest rate, and is ready to sign as <pb facs="0624" n="612"
                        xml:id="pg612"/> soon as Guinle receives the Brazilian Government’s
                    authority. The texts of the letters agreed to by Jones and Guinle are being
                    transmitted by separate telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
